  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -61,14 +61,14 @@ The following bugs have been fixed:\n \n * Wireshark crashes when run under Visual Studio on Windows. https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/work_items/21251[Work item 24787].\n \n-* Welcome page slide preferences are now available in the preferences window.\n+* Welcome page slide preferences are now available in the preferences window. {notable}\n \n * vwr: Read of uninitialized memory in pntoh16. wsbuglink:16460[].\n * vwr: Read of uninitialized memory in find_signature. wsbuglink:16461[].\n-* Upgrades on Windows do not retain existing optional features unless explicitly requested, resulting in accidental removal of features. wsbuglink:18925[].\n+* Upgrades on Windows do not retain existing optional features unless explicitly requested, resulting in accidental removal of features. wsbuglink:18925[]. {notable}\n * Wireshark.exe version 4.6.5 is twice as large as version 4.6.4. wsbuglink:21233[].\n * MACsec dissector global-buffer-overflow. wsbuglink:21235[].\n-* Wireshark 4.6.5 does not run on Windows 10 version 1809 (including Server 2019 and some LTSC versions) wsbuglink:21237[].\n+* Wireshark 4.6.5 does not run on Windows 10 version 1809 (including Server 2019 and some LTSC versions) wsbuglink:21237[]. {notable}\n * Fuzz job issue: fuzz-2026-05-02-14184750352.pcap. wsbuglink:21240[].\n * packet-bacapp: rename aurth-request to auth-request. wsbuglink:21246[].\n * Fuzz job issue: randpkt-2026-05-10-14293434231.pcap. wsbuglink:21253[].\n@@ -101,6 +101,7 @@ There are no new protocols in this release.\n BACapp\n BPv7\n DB/IB GDS DB\n+Kafka\n MACsec\n PFCP\n RF4CE\n",
